       All of these functions return the integer OOKK  upon  successful  comple‐
       tion.   (SVr4  specifies only “an integer value other than EERRRR”) If un‐
       successful, they return EERRRR.

       X/Open defines no error conditions.

       In this implementation, these functions return an error

       •   if the window pointer is null,

       •   if its timeout expires without having any data, or

       •   if the associated call to wwggeettcchh failed.

       This implementation provides an extension as well.  If a  SSIIGGWWIINNCCHH  in‐
       terrupts the function, it will return KKEEYY__RREESSIIZZEE rather than OOKK or EERRRR.

       Functions  prefixed with “mv” first perform cursor movement and fail if
       the position (_y, _x) is outside the window boundaries.

